## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates governance design capabilities for small remote teams, focusing on beginner-friendly processes that balance innovation with stability; emphasizes risk management, stakeholder communication, and scalable automation.

## Key Concepts
- Semantic versioning methodology
- Deprecation policy frameworks
- Automated compatibility testing
- Feature flag rollbacks
- Partner communication protocols

## Code Example
```javascript
// Version compatibility validator
function isCompatible(currentVersion, targetVersion) {
  const [cMA, cMi, cPa] = currentVersion.split('.').map(Number);
  const [tMA, tMi, tPa] = targetVersion.split('.').map(Number);

  // Major version changes are breaking
  if (cMA !== tMA) return false;

  // Minor version changes are backward compatible
  if (cMi > tMi) return false;

  return true;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a scalable reliability program that balances incident response with feature velocity and ROI.

## Key Concepts

- Platform vs product team governance
- SRE metrics: SLOs, error budgets, MTTR, and availability
- Incident playbooks, runbooks, blameless postmortems
- Auto-remediation, circuit breakers, canaries, multi-region failover
- ROI linkage and cost avoidance through reliability investments

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal auto-remediation skeleton
function autoRemediate(incident) {
  if (incident.severity === 'critical') {
    activateFailover();
  } else if (incident.type === 'timeout') {
    triggerCircuitBreaker();
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you prove ROI for reliability initiatives over time?
- Which metrics and milestones would you track to adjust SLOs?

